 "meta": {
  "name": "Input → persona determination matrix",
  "version": "0.1",
  "flag": "illustrative — weights are design seeds, calibrate before production",
  "closes": "F2",
  "method": "Persona posterior = softmax over per-column evidence sums. Hard priors (sex · age · life-stage · requires) zero out impossible columns BEFORE the soft evidence is summed, so e.g. a pregnancy column can never light up for a male. Many-to-many by construction: one signal supports several personas, and each persona is supported by many signals. A signal's value comes from a question answer (Appendix E), a derived flag, or a wearable/lab threshold.",
  "links": [
   "Doc 08",
   "Doc 05",
   "Appendix D",
   "Appendix E",
   "Appendix F"
  ]
 },
